dependent systems reveals geometric structure that is often overlooked when analysis is restricted to statistical or information}{\f6\fs22\lang1033
\_}{\f4\fs22\lang1033
theoretic descriptions. This work introduces a temporal}{\f6\fs22\lang1033
\_}{\f4\fs22\lang1033
geometry framework that treats entropy as a trajectory embedded in a symbolic manifold, allowing nonlinear transitions, bifurcations, and emergent patterns to be characterized with higher resolution than conventional approaches. By constructing multi}{\f6\fs22\lang1033
